                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1037-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="1037-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="1037-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ></span>Audio-Technica AT4049b</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The AT4049b is a revision of the company&#8217;s earlier mic, the AT4049a. Both are transformerless &#8220;pencil&#8221; microphones that accept interchangeable capsules. The 4049 is nominally an Omnidirectional microphone, but with appropriate capsules would support other patterns.</p><p>The preamp body, part number AT4900b-48, is common to these microphones:</p><ul><li>AT4900b-48 body + AT4051b-EL cardioid capsule = AT4051b</li><li>AT4900b-48 body + AT4049b-EL omni capsule = AT4049b</li><li>AT4900b-48 body + AT4053b-EL hyper capsule = AT4053b</li></ul><p></p><p><em>What is the difference between the AT4049a and AT4049b?</em></p><ul><li>The omni capsule in the &#8216;b&#8217; revision matches the sensitivity of the other &#8216;b&#8217; capsules. In the &#8216;a&#8217; revision, the Omni capsule had ~3dB higher sensitivity.</li><li>The AT4049b has a less pronounced HF presence peak, but less smooth HF response overall.</li><li>Self-noise has been cut from 19dBA to 16dBA on the AT4049b.</li><li>The AT4049b includes a -10dB pad, raising the max SPL from 146dB to 155dB.</li><li>The AT4049b is RoHS certified (free of hazardous substances).</li><li>The AT4049b has better EMI/RFI shielding.</li><li>Impedance has dropped from 100&Omega; to 50&Omega;.</li><li>The &#8216;b&#8217; revision is 7g heavier.</li></ul><p>The &#8216;b&#8217; series mics &#8212; the AT4051b, AT4053b, AT4049b &#8212; include two recessed switches on the mic body; one controls the pad, and the other controls the high-pass filter.</p><p>The mic ships with a clip (A-T p/n AT8405a), a foam windscreen, and a carrying case (p/n S1).<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audio-Technica/AT4049b">Audio-Technica AT4049b</a> is also known as: AT4049.</p>
